But note: In index.html, the first radio input has id="reminder"? Wait line: `<input class="govuk-radios__input" id="reminder" name="reminder" type="radio" value="email" data-aria-controls="conditional-reminder">`. Yes.

Second radio: `id="reminder-2"` value="text" data-aria-controls="conditional-reminder-2"

Third radio: inside optout-radios: `id="reminder-none"` value="none" (no data-aria-controls)

Thus step sequence: Seek "#reminder" -> focus on email radio.

Then press ArrowDown twice: First arrow down moves focus to next radio in DOM order? Let's check ordering: After email radio (#reminder), next sibling is the conditional div? Actually structure: Within channel-radios div, we have:

<div class="govuk-radios__item">
  <input id="reminder"...>
  <label...>
</div>
<div class="govuk-radios__conditional ... id="conditional-reminder">...</div>

<div class="govuk-radios__item">
